 * double-cell lookback pass) is what makes them renderable. The tier rides
 * {@see SymbolMap::withKana()} or the `wide` selector class; the default
 * corpus and every byte-frozen render digest stay untouched until then.
 *
 * Chafa selects this tier through the WIDE tag (get_default_tags_for_char
 * derives WIDE from g_unichar_iswide for the block, ALPHA from isalpha, and
 * no NARROW), which is exactly the effective-tag derivation in
 * {@see SymbolMap::defaultTagsFor()} below.
 *
 * Generated verbatim from chafa @413b76e4d
 * chafa/internal/chafa-symbols-kana.h (181 entries, TAG_NONE declared).
 *
 * Mirrors chafa.ChafaSymbolSetKana (chafa/internal/chafa-symbols-kana.h).
 */
